title 52V battery near empty (48V resting), level 9: a 3 s climb sags it to 44V

# 14s pack: 58.8V full, 42V cutoff. The low-voltage limit eases power off
# between 44.8V and 43.3V. Upstream it acted on the lowest voltage seen, so
# one sag on a climb kept power reduced until the controller restarted.
# Now it recovers (slowly, and only under load) once the sag is over.
config max_battery_x100v 5880
config low_cut_off_v 42

at 0 level 9
at 0 voltage 48
at 1000 cadence 70 over 500
at 5000 voltage 44
at 8000 voltage 48
at 30000 cadence 0

end 31000

# 26.7A before the sag, limited during it, back to 26.7A within 2 s of it
# ending. (Upstream stayed at 21.3A, 71%, for the rest of the ride.)
expect 4900 current == 89
expect 7900 current < 89
expect 10000 current == 89
expect 29900 current == 89
